#: README.md:45
msgid "The basics"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:47
msgid ""
"When using PyCV the user will need to create a module[^1] that must at least"
" contain an initialization dictionary and a calculate function"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:49
msgid ""
"[^1]: a module is a `.py` file or a directory that contains a `__init__.py`,"
" here we will only show `py` files"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:51
msgid "What to write in the plumed.dat (PYCVINTERFACE)"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:57 README.md:75
msgid ""
"`IMPORT` this is the only mandatory keyword, this indicates the python "
"module to load"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:58 README.md:76
msgid ""
"`INIT` indicates the function to call at initialization. Defaults to "
"`plumedInit`"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:59 README.md:77
msgid "`COMPONENTS` can be specified either in python or in the plumed.dat"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:60
msgid "`NOPBC` can be specified either in python or in the plumed.dat"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:61
msgid ""
"`ATOMS`, `GROUPA`,`GROUPB`, using `GROUP*` will make plumed set up a "
"neighbor list between the groups, or group A, whereas with ATOMS all the "
"atom will be passed"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:62
msgid ""
"`PAIR`,`NLIST`,`NL_CUTOFF`,`NL_STRIDE` can only be specified in the "
"plumed.dat ~to be verified~"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:63 README.md:78
msgid ""
"`CALCULATE` indicates the function to call at calculate time. Defaults to "
"`plumedCalculate`"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:64
msgid ""
"`PREPARE` indicates the function to call at prepare time. Ignored if not "
"specified"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:65
msgid ""
"`UPDATE` indicates the function to call at update time. Ignored if not "
"specified"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:67
msgid "What to write in the plumed.dat (PYFUNCTION)"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:79
msgid "`ARG` the list of arguments, to be specified in the plumed.dat"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:81
msgid ""
"PYFUNCTION is simpler: but needs to get the arguments from the plumed object"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:93
msgid "The functions"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:95
msgid ""
"For both PYFUNCTION and PYCVINTERFACE the function called by plumed must "
"accept a specific object."
msgstr ""

#: README.md:96
msgid ""
"PYCVINTERFACE functions will expect a "
"`plumedCommunications.PythonCVInterface` object"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:97
msgid ""
"PYFUNCTION functions will expect a `plumedCommunications.PythonFunction` "
"object"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:99
msgid ""
"These objects are used to retrieve data and settings from plumed. Plumed "
"will get data back with the `data` attribute (see [below](#the-data-"
"attribute)) but mainly with the use of returned dictionaries."
msgstr ""

#: README.md:101
msgid ""
"In the [examples](examples.md#getting-the-manual) I show how to retrieve the"
" manual for those objects"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:104
msgid "Initialization"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:106
msgid ""
"If in the plumed.dat `INIT` is not specified, plumed will search for an "
"object \"plumedInit\", that can be either a function that returns a dict or "
"a dict This dict MUST contain at least the information about the presence of"
" the derivatives and on the periodicity of the variable. We will refer to "
"this dict as \"the _init dict_\" from now."
msgstr ""

#: README.md:112
msgid ""
"The _init dict_ will tell plumed how many components the calculate function "
"will return and how they shall behave. Along this the dict can contain all "
"the keyword that are compatible with PYCVINTERFACE. Mind that if the same "
"keyword is specified both in the _init dict_ and in the plumed file the "
"calculation will be aborted to avoid unwanted settings conflicts. In case of"
" flags the dict entry must be a boolean, differently from the standard "
"plumed input."
msgstr ""

#: README.md:122
msgid ""
"The only keyword that can only be specified in python is `COMPONENTS`. The "
"`COMPONENTS` key must point to a dict that has as keys the names of the "
"components. Each component dictionary must have two keys:"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:126
msgid ""
"`\"period\"`: `None` of a list of two values, min and max (like `[0,1]` or "
"also strings like `[\"0.5*pi\",\"2*pi\"]`)"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:128
msgid ""
"`\"derivative\"`: `True` or `False` If you want to use a single component "
"you can create the `\"COMPONENTS\"` dict with as single key, the name will "
"be ignored. In the previous example the key `\"Value\"` is used instead of "
"`\"COMPONENTS\"`: it is a shorter form for `\"COMPONENTS\":{\"any\":{...}}`."
" To avoid confusion you cannot specify both `\"COMPONENTS\"` and `\"Value\"`"
" in the same dict."
msgstr ""

#: README.md:136
msgid ""
"To speed up the declarations of the components the `plumedCommunications` "
"module contains a submodule `defaults` with the default dictionaries already"
" set up:"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:138
msgid ""
"`plumedCommunications.defaults.COMPONENT={\"period\":None, "
"\"derivative\":True}`"
msgstr ""
"`plumedCommunications.defaults.COMPONENT={\"period\":None, "
"\"derivative\":True}`"

#: README.md:139
msgid ""
"`plumedCommunications.defaults.COMPONENT_NODEV={\"period\":None, "
"\"derivative\":False}`"
msgstr ""
"`plumedCommunications.defaults.COMPONENT_NODEV={\"period\":None, "
"\"derivative\":False}`"

#: README.md:141
msgid "Calculate"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:143
msgid ""
"If `CALCULATE` is not specified, plumed will search for a function named "
"\"plumedCalculate\" plumed will read the variable returned accordingly to "
"what it was specified in the initialization dict."
msgstr ""

#: README.md:147
msgid ""
"The calculate function must, as all the other functions accept a "
"`plumedCommunications.PythonCVInterface` (or a "
"`plumedCommunications.PythonFunction` in case of a pyfunction) object as "
"only input."
msgstr ""

#: README.md:150
msgid ""
"The calculate function must either return a float or a tuple or, in the case"
" of multiple components, a dict whose keys are the name of the components, "
"whose elements are either float or tuple."
msgstr ""

#: README.md:154
msgid ""
"Plumed will assign automatically the result to the CV (to the key named "
"element), if the name of the component is missing the calculation will be "
"interrupted with an error message. If derivatives are disabled it will "
"expect a float(or a double). In case of activated derivatives it will "
"interrupt the calculation if the return value would not be a tuple. The "
"tuple should be (float, ndArray(nat,3),ndArray(3,3)) with the first elements"
" the value, the second the atomic derivatives and the third the box "
"derivative (that can also have shape(9), with format (x_x, x_y, x_z, y_x, "
"y_y, y_z, z_x, z_y, z_z)), if the box derivative are not present a WARNING "
"will be raised, but the calculation won't be interrupted."
msgstr ""

#: README.md:166
msgid "Prepare"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:168
msgid ""
"If the `PREPARE` keyword is used, the defined function will be called at "
"prepare time, before calculate. The returned \"prepare\" dictionary can "
"contain a `\"setAtomRequest\"` key with a parseable ATOM string, like in the"
" standard plumed input (or a list of indexes, 0 based)."
msgstr ""

#: README.md:180
msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:182
msgid ""
"If the `UPDATE` keyword is used, the defined function will be called at "
"update time, after calculate. As now plumed will ignore the return of this "
"function (but it stills need to return a dict) and it is intended to "
"accumulate things or post process data afer calculate"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:187
msgid ""
"In the example `plmdAction.data[\"pycv\"]=0` is initialized in `pyinit` and "
"its value is updated in calculate."
msgstr ""

#: README.md:191
msgid "The `data` attribute"
msgstr ""

#: README.md:192
msgid ""
"The plumedCommunications.PythonCVInterface has a `data` attribute that is a "
"dictionary and can be used to store data during the calculations"
msgstr ""
